$Aeon::Books["yKarma","cntnt"] = "<f2>Karma<f1> is the law of responcibility of one's own actions. In lamens terms, 'What goes around, comes around', however, there is more to it than just that. The Law of Karma states that for every action, there is a corresponding reaction, depending on the frame of mind the action was executed in. Any action that is accompanied by thoughts of <f3>Craving<f1>, <f3>Resistance<f1>, or <f3>Delusion<f1> will always be an <f3>Unskillful<f1> one, which is commonly percieved as 'Bad' or 'Evil'. Contrary, any action not accompanied by any of those thoughts, is a <f2>Skillful<f1> action, also commonly percieved as 'Good'. To obtain Karma, one must participate in actions of Skillful or Unskillful nature, but with this elevation of Karma, also comes knowledge and increased levels of <f2>Skill<f1>. To obtain Karma you must use skills, in skillful or unskillful ways, you can start by Hunting Meteors! For every level of Karma, negative or positive, you gain a <f2>Skill Point<f1> that may be used on any skills that you have obtained <f2>Knowledge<f1> of. You can find out more about Skill Points by reading '<f2>Skills<f1>'. Unskillful actions are always easier to commit, however, they are also easier to undo... If one with a negative level of Karma is apprehended or thrown in Prison, they must sit in seclusion serving their sentance, the whole while having their Karma tic upward to zero. So make sure you stay out of trouble, and remember, 'What goes around, comes around'!";